{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"flamboyant-possessive-blackbuck","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nConstruction-time or preview-time repair would violate read-only commands. Retirement completion is safe only after operation config is frozen, provider preflight and exclusive ownership succeed, and under-lock staleness validation passes.\n\n## Outcome\nInvoke the S3 recovery operation once at the validated write-bearing reconcile boundary before remote observation; every read-only or filtered path remains zero-write.\n\n## Plan\n1. Add spies around repository save and `os.replace` for construction, load, reconcile-check, dry-run, preview, selection, filtering, and live passes.\n2. Place recovery after immutable operation snapshot, preflight, exclusive pass ownership, and staleness validation, but before remote issue fetch, binding walk, differ, or lifecycle mutation.\n3. Treat a durable tombstone as authoritative until explicit `unretire`; automatic 200, `clear_absent`, or same-key confirmation cannot revoke it.\n4. On completion failure, abort before remote observation and preserve the overlap for retry.\n\n## Testing\nOrder-spy tests pin each predecessor/successor and zero provider calls on recovery failure. Read-only tables assert zero replacement calls.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A live write-bearing pass completes exact recovery after all validation gates and before its first remote observation.\n- [ ] Construction, load, check, dry-run, preview, selection, and filtered paths perform zero recovery writes.\n- [ ] Recovery failure performs zero remote calls and preserves recoverable evidence.\n- [ ] Automatic success/reset/same-key confirmation does not override the tombstone.\n- [ ] Explicit `unretire` removes the tombstone and therefore removes the completion candidate.\n\n## Out of scope\nRich-emission caller cutover and ADR finalization.","id":"90a5-6a33-5cda-4064","parent_id":"486a-69ef-6370-48ff","priority":1,"tags":["rp02","binding-recovery","tdd"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-02 S3 T2 — Invoke recovery only at the validated write boundary"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787027694151845001,"uuid":"d814f485-d304-4c25-9513-1e6e6e380c91"}